import{_ as a,o as t,c as o,ak as n}from"./chunks/framework.B8jO0odJ.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"Chainy blockchain visual design handoff","description":"Status: generated concept assets for the updated GDD; not screenshots, playable scenes, or Unity-import-ready UI.\\nCreated: 22 October 2026.\\nGeneration: built-in imagegen; no f","frontmatter":{"title":"Chainy blockchain visual design handoff","description":"Status: generated concept assets for the updated GDD; not screenshots, playable scenes, or Unity-import-ready UI.\\nCreated: 22 October 2026.\\nGeneration: built-in imagegen; no f","source":"docs/media/gdd/gameplay-first/notes/visual-blockchain-notes.md","category":"Other documents","sourceUpdated":"2026-10-22T22:46:54+08:00","outline":[2,3]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"content/docs/media/gdd/gameplay-first/notes/visual-blockchain-notes.md","filePath":"content/docs/media/gdd/gameplay-first/notes/visual-blockchain-notes.md"}'),r={name:"content/docs/media/gdd/gameplay-first/notes/visual-blockchain-notes.md"};function i(s,e,l,c,d,h){return t(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<div><h1 id="chainy-blockchain-visual-design-handoff">Chainy blockchain visual design handoff<a class="header-anchor" href="#chainy-blockchain-visual-design-handoff" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h1><p>Status: generated concept assets for the updated GDD; not screenshots, playable scenes, or Unity-import-ready UI. Created: 22 October 2026. Generation: built-in image_gen; no fallback CLI. Reference review: current isometric exploration and dialogue-overlay images under O:/Documents/GitHub/Chainy/docs/media/gdd/current-visuals/. The older Blocky name is deliberately replaced by Matthew.</p><h2 id="assets">Assets<a class="header-anchor" href="#assets" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h2><h3 id="blockchain-worldpng">blockchain-world.png<a class="header-anchor" href="#blockchain-worldpng" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h3><ul><li>Output: docs/media/gdd/gameplay-first/blockchain-world.png</li><li>Purpose/caption: <strong>Blockchain World — a compact beacon restoration route.</strong> Matthew introduces a damaged local ledger, a verified-copy terminal and a stale-copy terminal. The learner examines evidence before restoring the beacon.</li><li>Composition: orthographic isometric, approximately 40-degree downward view, faceted stone/grass, muted olive/sand/navy palette, restrained cyan/amber glow; blue-haired yellow-clad explorer and white screen-faced Matthew.</li><li>Level intent: central introduction checkpoint; left amber local terminal; right cyan verification terminal; lower gray stale-copy terminal; beacon above. The four props are not four required consensus participants.</li><li>Feedback must use text/icons in the actual game; environment color is supplemental.</li><li>No claim that the player&#39;s action edits accepted global history or that the scene represents a real distributed network.</li></ul><h3 id="blockchain-repairpng">blockchain-repair.png<a class="header-anchor" href="#blockchain-repairpng" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h3><ul><li>Output: docs/media/gdd/gameplay-first/blockchain-repair.png</li><li>Purpose/caption: <strong>Repair the local copy using references and evidence.</strong> Arrange B after trusted A, then C after B. Compare the altered payment with the verified record; distinguish a wrong value from a missing latest block.</li><li>UI intent: a modal overlay pauses world movement. Cards support dragging AND tap-card/tap-slot interaction. Check order explains the first broken reference without removing currency or erasing progress. View evidence opens the trusted source/checkpoint.</li><li>Verified transaction: portable Lantern #014, payment 8 + fee 1, owner Explorer. The altered copy records payment 6; the stale copy lacks the latest block.</li><li>Symbolic A/B/C reference labels are visibly disclosed. They are not cryptographic hashes. If the implemented lesson uses actual hashes, recompute full values internally and present shortened display values with disclosure.</li><li>No all-nodes-instantly-synchronized assertion. Restoring this checkpoint is a game objective, not a universal consensus algorithm.</li><li>The first UI generation mistakenly used a beacon-like lantern thumbnail. A targeted edit replaced only the thumbnail with portable brass-and-glass equipment. The corrected variant is the delivered file.</li></ul><h2 id="visual-qa-and-production-caveats">Visual QA and production caveats<a class="header-anchor" href="#visual-qa-and-production-caveats" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h2><ul><li>Both selected PNGs inspected visually after generation; 1672 × 941 pixels, RGB landscape.</li><li>Matthew spelling, local-copy framing, payment 8 plus fee 1, altered value 6, stale-copy explanation and A/B/C symbolic disclaimer are correct in the selected UI.</li><li>Colors are accompanied by words and distinct warning/clock icons.</li><li>Generated text is baked into the mockup. Production UI requires separate editable components, real font assets, safe-area checks, localization, and actual target-device touch/readability tests.</li><li>The overlay is illustrative and information-dense for small phones: production may reveal evidence in a separate tab/sheet while preserving the same learning action.</li><li>Include a visible close/back control and focus handling in implementation; the concept&#39;s limited button set is not an exhaustive navigation specification.</li><li>Asset licensing/provenance: AI-generated concepts produced for this task; no external stock or game assets copied. Team must review final production assets and fonts before distribution.</li><li>Proposed import: reference/documentation PNG only, not a full-screen runtime texture requirement. Do not infer runtime polygon, texture-memory or performance budgets from the concepts.</li><li>No measured Android performance or learner usability claims.</li></ul><h2 id="exact-prompts">Exact prompts<a class="header-anchor" href="#exact-prompts" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h2><h3 id="world-generation">World generation<a class="header-anchor" href="#world-generation" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h3><p>Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: Chainy educational mobile game GDD environment concept, landscape 16:9. Primary request: a compact Blockchain Beacon island level; concept artwork, not an actual game screenshot. Scene: angular pale stone ruins, grassy faceted ledges, calm deep blue water and short stone paths. Three local ledger stations clearly distributed around a central damaged beacon: a dim amber beacon terminal, a cyan verification terminal, and a softly outlined inactive verification terminal. These represent a local training simulation, not worldwide blockchain nodes. A readable route connects the three stations, with no excessive sprawling environment. Subjects: a small blue-haired explorer wearing a mustard-yellow jacket and backpack, facing Matthew, a friendly white faceted robot with a black screen face and cyan eyes. Small full bodies readable in gameplay, not oversized mascot portraits. Camera/style: fixed orthographic isometric camera viewed downward at about 40 degrees. Restrained stylized low-poly faceted geometry, angular stone silhouettes, sparse painterly detail, long soft directional shadows, modest cyan emission, muted olive greens, stone sand, dark navy water. Consistent faceted character style, no toy plastic, no rounded clay miniature, no voxel blocks, no third-person over-shoulder view. Composition: central play space with explorer and Matthew, damaged beacon on an elevated rear platform, secondary verification stations reached by clear left/right paths. Enough negative space around interaction stations to be usable as a compact game level blockout reference. Text: only small simple corner label &quot;BLOCKCHAIN WORLD&quot; and sublabel &quot;Concept design&quot;. No floating paragraph UI, no illegible fake labels, no hash strings, no currency logos. Constraints: no mining rocks, no wealth imagery, no real brands, no copying another game&#39;s assets. No implication that one player edits global history. 3D environment/art direction proposal only.</p><h3 id="repair-overlay-generation">Repair overlay generation<a class="header-anchor" href="#repair-overlay-generation" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h3><p>Input edit target: selected blockchain-world.png. Use case: ui-mockup. Edit the supplied Blockchain World concept by adding a legible landscape mobile-game interaction overlay. Keep the faceted isometric island, blue-haired yellow-clad explorer and white cyan-eyed robot as a softly dimmed background. This is a high-fidelity UI CONCEPT, not a finished screenshot. Primary request: an educational local ledger repair interface, generous large type, a navy panel and pale-cyan borders, high contrast, readable labels, rounded corners only on UI. Keep island visible around panel edges. No on-screen movement controls while panel is open. Exact interface structure: Header &quot;REPAIR LOCAL COPY&quot; with small subtitle &quot;Matthew • Blockchain beacon&quot;. A sequence row with three large outlined slots: &quot;Trusted A&quot; then right-arrow then &quot;?&quot; then right-arrow then &quot;?&quot;. Below the row instruction &quot;Match each previous reference.&quot; Two draggable cards underneath, deliberately out of order: Left card: &quot;Record C&quot; then &quot;Previous: B&quot;. Right card: &quot;Record B&quot; then &quot;Previous: A&quot;. Small note below the cards: &quot;A, B, C are symbolic reference labels.&quot; Separate right-side verified record panel with exact text: &quot;VERIFIED RECORD&quot; &quot;Lantern #014&quot; &quot;Payment 8 + fee 1&quot; &quot;Owner: Explorer&quot; At bottom of main panel two clearly separate compact status tiles, differentiated by both icon and words: Triangle warning icon, amber accent, text &quot;Altered copy&quot; / &quot;Payment 6 differs from verified 8&quot;. Clock icon, gray-blue accent, text &quot;Stale copy&quot; / &quot;Missing the latest block&quot;. Bottom button &quot;Check order&quot; and secondary button &quot;View evidence&quot;. Small outside footer label &quot;Concept design&quot;. Keep card ordering and error distinction clear; do not include hashes or imply symbolic A/B/C are actual cryptographic hashes. This is recovering a local corrupted display from a trusted source, not rewriting accepted global history. No global consensus claim. No additional text, invented paragraphs, overlapping text or logos. Leave ample margins. The learning action is arranging records by previous reference and comparing a changed payment against verified evidence.</p><h3 id="targeted-thumbnail-correction">Targeted thumbnail correction<a class="header-anchor" href="#targeted-thumbnail-correction" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h3><p>Input edit target: original repair overlay generation. Change only the illustration inside the right-side VERIFIED RECORD panel. Replace the miniature stone beacon-on-island illustration with a small portable handheld brass-and-glass lantern, a practical equipment item with a carry handle, warm amber light and simple faceted low-poly design. It must have no island base, grass, stone plinth or ruins. Keep its existing scale and position in the panel. Preserve every word, number, punctuation, UI element, color, layout, background, character and all other pixels as closely as possible. In particular preserve &quot;Lantern #014&quot;, &quot;Payment 8 + fee 1&quot;, &quot;Owner: Explorer&quot;, and the symbolic reference disclaimer. This is the NFT equipment the explorer purchased, not the world beacon.</p><h2 id="supplemental-shared-navigation-sheet">Supplemental shared navigation sheet<a class="header-anchor" href="#supplemental-shared-navigation-sheet" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h2><h3 id="navigation-journalpng">navigation-journal.png<a class="header-anchor" href="#navigation-journalpng" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h3><ul><li>Output: docs/media/gdd/gameplay-first/navigation-journal.png</li><li>Dimensions: 1672 x 941 pixels.</li><li>Caption: <strong>Three separate screen studies: world selection, chronological quest guidance and the learning journal.</strong> Web3 opens first; Blockchain and AI explain their prerequisites. The quest log distinguishes a restoration goal from its next task and completed history. Encyclopedia progress records exposure and practice, not a mastery percentage.</li><li>Confirmed text: Web3 / Open / Enter; Blockchain / Finish Web3; AI / Finish Blockchain; current goal Restore workshop; next step Buy lantern; completed Meet Sean; Wallet / Manage keys and approve transactions.; Discovered / Explained / Practiced / New situation.</li><li>Visual QA: labels are readable, world order is correct, guide name Sean is correct, back chevrons are present, no teacher data or mastery percentage is shown.</li><li>Correction performed: removed a misleading arrow from the next-task card to completed history. The current-goal-to-next-task arrow remains.</li><li>These are side-by-side GDD studies, NOT the proposed phone orientation or simultaneous three-pane in-game layout. Implement each as a separate responsive screen/panel, with landscape phone adaptation and device tests.</li><li>Encyclopedia stages reflect collected learning evidence. A correct response does not establish durable mastery; New situation means a transfer challenge, not certification.</li><li>All text and controls need editable Unity implementation. The large sheet is not intended as a single runtime UI texture.</li></ul><h3 id="exact-navigation-sheet-prompt">Exact navigation sheet prompt<a class="header-anchor" href="#exact-navigation-sheet-prompt" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h3><p>Use case: ui-mockup. Asset type: Chainy educational mobile-game GDD shared interface concept sheet; landscape 16:9. Primary request: three separate screen studies side by side, clearly labeled as three separate UI screens for comparison, NOT three windows shown simultaneously on one phone. Equal-width study panels, generous spacing and minimal readable text. A thin outer sheet heading says &quot;SHARED NAVIGATION&quot;; subtitle &quot;Three separate screen studies&quot;. Common style: navy overlays with restrained cyan borders, high-contrast white sans-serif type, muted pale-cyan secondary text, simple consistent line icons. Behind each screen, a faint faceted orthographic isometric island scene of angular stone, olive grass and blue water. Avoid tiny text, ornate decoration, toy-plastic rounded landscape, busy fake HUD, teacher data, progress/mastery percentages. LEFT SCREEN: header &quot;WORLD SELECT&quot;. Three large vertical cards with simple island/gateway icons. Card1 &quot;Web3&quot; with state &quot;Open&quot; and button &quot;Enter&quot;. Card2 &quot;Blockchain&quot; with clear lock icon and state &quot;Finish Web3&quot;. Card3 &quot;AI&quot; with clear lock icon and state &quot;Finish Blockchain&quot;. Sequential arrows subtly connect cards downward. MIDDLE SCREEN: header &quot;QUEST LOG&quot; with simple book/checklist icon. A highlighted navy/cyan card reads &quot;CURRENT GOAL&quot; then &quot;Restore workshop&quot;. Under it a smaller connected card reads &quot;NEXT STEP&quot; then &quot;Buy lantern&quot;. Under that a checkmark row reads &quot;COMPLETED&quot; then &quot;Meet Sean&quot;. The hierarchy must clearly mean restore workshop is the overall goal and buying a lantern is its next task, not a contradictory quest order. RIGHT SCREEN: header &quot;ENCYCLOPEDIA&quot; with simple book icon. Entry name &quot;Wallet&quot; with a wallet icon. One short definition: &quot;Manage keys and approve transactions.&quot; A vertical learning journey has four rows exactly: &quot;Discovered&quot;, &quot;Explained&quot;, &quot;Practiced&quot;, &quot;New situation&quot;. Discovered has a checkmark; Explained is the current highlighted row; Practiced and New situation are future outlined rows. No numeric mastery label. At bottom small button &quot;Practice next&quot;. Each screen includes a small simple back-chevron at the top. Small outer footer &quot;Concept design • UI text and controls rebuilt in Unity&quot;. Constraints: reproduce requested text accurately, no invented descriptions or guide names, no real currency or branding, no teacher dashboard. These are concept studies, not actual screenshots. Keep the separate panel edges obvious.</p><h3 id="exact-navigation-sheet-correction-prompt">Exact navigation sheet correction prompt<a class="header-anchor" href="#exact-navigation-sheet-correction-prompt" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h3><p>Make one precise UI correction only: remove the cyan downward arrow between the middle QUEST LOG panel&#39;s &quot;NEXT STEP / Buy lantern&quot; card and the &quot;COMPLETED / Meet Sean&quot; card. Leave the empty gap, so the completed-history row is clearly not a future step. Preserve the earlier arrow between &quot;CURRENT GOAL / Restore workshop&quot; and &quot;NEXT STEP / Buy lantern&quot;. Preserve all other words, images, positions, colors, controls, borders, backgrounds, shapes and pixels as closely as possible. Do not add any new label or icon.</p></div>',1)])])}const m=a(r,[["render",i]]);export{p as __pageData,m as default};
